                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not too deep into PCIe device inventories or how those are used in redfish, listing a concrete use-case\n\ne.g. \"for implementing redfish resource X this change is needed because... \"\n\ncould make a stronger case for this change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thang Tran",
                        "email": "thuutran@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "thangtran-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I updated as your suggestion."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Showing a object tree layout could be helpful here.\nSince there's multiple functions, the `PCIeDevice` interface would likely go on multiple object paths, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thang Tran",
                        "email": "thuutran@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "thangtran-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I added the object tree layout. \n\n>Since there's multiple functions, the PCIeDevice interface would likely go on multiple object paths, right?\n\nThe PCIe device object has only 1 PCIeDevice interface. But other dbus object paths that includes PCIeFunction interface are created to show PCIe functions's properties. If this PCIe device is multiple function, multiple object paths that inlcude PCIeFunction interface will be created"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Are there patches up for updating other applications to\nexpose / consume the newly defined interface.\n\nIMO it would make sense to link to those or make a `TODO` section here in case this change is in design phase. Or making a topic with those changes.\n\nTo give some idea of all the things that need changing before the deprecated properties can be removed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Thang Tran",
                        "email": "thuutran@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "thangtran-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "I added the link to the source code need to be updated and move to `TODO` section."
                }
            ],
